{
    "name": "E2E Shopify - Updated Checkout Trigger",
    "description": "Updated Checkout fires when a checkout in the online store changes (manual storefront step).",
    "notes": {
        "bac45c97-0a44-4ca7-8834-779a19505416": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": -128,
            "width": 400,
            "height": 400,
            "content": "## ⚠️ Manual E2E — requires a storefront action\n\n`checkouts/update` cannot be provoked through the Admin API — only a real storefront checkout session fires it.\n\n### How to test\n1. Start this flow (the webhook is registered on start).\n2. Open the online store in an **incognito window** (https://<store>.myshopify.com; the dev-store password is in Online Store → Preferences). A fresh window forces a NEW checkout session — a reused window resumes the previous checkout instead.\n3. Add a product to the cart and click through to the checkout page — creating the checkout session fires **checkouts/create**;\n4. then enter the **email address and shipping address** and continue to the payment step — each contact/address change fires **checkouts/update**.\n\nThe Assert checks the checkout token and topic. A checkout Shopify does not list as abandoned yet (no contact details entered) is emitted with its token only; once listed it carries the full abandoned checkout. AfterAll timeout is 600 s — finish the storefront steps within 10 minutes of starting the flow."
        }
    },
